<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Lemma 1</h2>

<div id="Thmrestatelemmax1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_restatelemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmrestatelemmax1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma</span></span><span id="Thmrestatelemmax1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Shift-invariance &amp; unconstrained AoC for Contrastive Loss). ‣ 3.2 Limitations of the Contrastive Loss ‣ 3 Problem Statement ‣ Optimizing What Matters: AUC-DrivenLearning for Robust Neural Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmrestatelemmax1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\tau}(s^{+},S^{-})\;=\;-\log\!\frac{e^{s^{+}/\tau}}{e^{s^{+}/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{s/\tau}},\qquad\tau&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\tau}(s^{+},S^{-})\;=\;-\log\!\frac{e^{s^{+}/\tau}}{e^{s^{+}/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{s/\tau}},\qquad\tau&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With notations of equation equation <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.2 Limitations of the Contrastive Loss ‣ 3 Problem Statement ‣ Optimizing What Matters: AUC-DrivenLearning for Robust Neural Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> the population loss can be rewritten as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s]\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\,q\sim\mathcal{Q},\;p^{+}\sim\mathcal{P}^{+}(\cdot\mid q),\{p^{-}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{P}^{-}(\cdot\mid q)\;}\!\Bigl[\,\ell_{\tau}\bigl(s(q,p^{+}),\,\{s(q,p^{-})\mid p^{-}\in\{p^{-}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\}\}\bigr)\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="1.400em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s]\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\,q\sim\mathcal{Q},\;p^{+}\sim\mathcal{P}^{+}(\cdot\mid q),\{p^{-}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{P}^{-}(\cdot\mid q)\;}\!\Bigl[\,\ell_{\tau}\bigl(s(q,p^{+}),\,\{s(q,p^{-})\mid p^{-}\in\{p^{-}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\}\}\bigr)\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmrestatelemmax1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Shift<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>invariance.</span><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any measurable offset </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\colon\mathcal{Q}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\colon\mathcal{Q}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
define the shifted scorer</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{g}(q,d)\;=\;s(q,d)+g(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{g}(q,d)\;=\;s(q,d)+g(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s_{g}]=\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s_{g}]=\mathcal{L}_{\tau}[s]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Arbitrary degradation of AoC.</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert s(q,d)\rvert\leq M&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert s(q,d)\rvert\leq M&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then for every
</span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> there exists an offset </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that the
Area</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">over</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ROC (AoC) defined as :</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{AoC}[s]\;=\;\Pr_{q_{1},q_{1}\sim\mathcal{Q},p^{+}\sim\mathcal{P}^{+}(.|q_{1}),p-\sim\mathcal{P}^{-}(.|q_{2})}\bigl[s(q_{1},p^{+})&lt;s(q_{2},p^{-})\bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>AoC</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{AoC}[s]\;=\;\Pr_{q_{1},q_{1}\sim\mathcal{Q},p^{+}\sim\mathcal{P}^{+}(.|q_{1}),p-\sim\mathcal{P}^{-}(.|q_{2})}\bigl[s(q_{1},p^{+})&lt;s(q_{2},p^{-})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{AoC}[s_{g}]\geq 0.5-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>AoC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{AoC}[s_{g}]\geq 0.5-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Hence global positive–negative separation can be made
arbitrarily poor without altering the Contrastive Loss.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(i) Shift<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>invariance.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and abbreviate
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=e^{s^{+}/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{s/\tau}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=e^{s^{+}/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{s/\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Adding <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(q)</annotation></semantics></math> to <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> score gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{g}=e^{(s^{+}+g)/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{(s+g)/\tau}=e^{g/\tau}Z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{g}=e^{(s^{+}+g)/\tau}+\sum_{s\in S^{-}}e^{(s+g)/\tau}=e^{g/\tau}Z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">while the numerator of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is also multiplied by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{g/\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{g/\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is unchanged and so is the expectation
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(ii) Arbitrary AoC degradation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw independent offsets <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(q)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(q)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For two independent samples <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{1},p^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{1},p^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{2},p^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{2},p^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{g}(q_{1},p^{+})-s_{g}(q_{2},p^{-})=\underbrace{s(q_{1},p^{+})-s(q_{2},p^{-})}_{\text{bounded by }2M}+\underbrace{g(q_{1})-g(q_{2})}_{\mathcal{N}(0,2\sigma^{2})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>bounded by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{g}(q_{1},p^{+})-s_{g}(q_{2},p^{-})=\underbrace{s(q_{1},p^{+})-s(q_{2},p^{-})}_{\text{bounded by }2M}+\underbrace{g(q_{1})-g(q_{2})}_{\mathcal{N}(0,2\sigma^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> the Gaussian term dominates, so
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[s_{g}(q_{1},p^{+})&lt;s_{g}(q_{2},p^{-})]\to 0.5." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[s_{g}(q_{1},p^{+})&lt;s_{g}(q_{2},p^{-})]\to 0.5.</annotation></semantics></math>
Choose <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> large enough that the probability exceeds
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; this yields the required <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ablation over Hard Negatives, LR, and Batch Size</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct controlled ablations on the sensitivity of training on three hyper parameters, namely the learning rate, batch size and number of hard negatives. Our study is limited to training on the MiniLM case. For brevity, we show the results with the best learning rate for each batch size.</p>
</div>
