<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The tables indicate that MW loss is rather stable with respect to changes in batch size and number of hard negative examples while CL loss is more sensitive.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Convergence analysis</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we provide results on the number of training steps until the the best checkpoint.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="A3.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training steps at best checkpoint</span> for each dataset and loss (MW vs CL), across model sizes.</figcaption>
